-- title:
--   Height equals dimension plus codimension, Cartier module form
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$, let $d$ be a natural number and let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: a $d$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, linear part $X_i + Y_i$, and satisfying the associativity identity, here assumed commutative in the sense that interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $h$ be a natural number, and assume that the quotient of the power series ring $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of $\Phi.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ p$, the $p$-fold iterated sum series $[p]_\Phi$ obtained by repeated substitution into the group law, has $k$-dimension $p^h$. The conclusion is that there exists $e$ with $d + e = h$ (so in particular $d \le h$) such that the following module admits a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,e$ over the ring $W(k)/(p)$: the quotient of $\overline M = M/\big((p)\cdot\top\big)$, where $M$ is the Cartier module [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule p Φ`](def/MvFormalGroup_CartierModule.html#L162) (tuples of power series in countably many variables with zero constant term, compatible with the Witt addition law and the group law), by the $W(k)/(p)$-span of the classes of the elements $\mathrm{frobenius}\,f$, $f \in M$, where $\mathrm{frobenius}$ is precomposition with the Verschiebung substitution family `WittLaw.verFam`.
--
--   This is the codimension formula for the Cartier–Dieudonné module of a commutative formal group law over a perfect field: for a formal group of dimension $d$ whose $p$-torsion has order $p^h$, the quotient $M/FM$ has $k$-dimension $h-d$. It feeds into the computation of the structure of $M/pM$ as a module over $W(k)/(p)$ recorded in [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.nonempty_basis_quotient_smul_top_of_finrank_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.nonempty_basis_quotient_smul_top_of_finrank_eq_pow).
